## Run

Python 3.10 or newer and an OpenGL 3.3 compatible graphics device are required.

```powershell
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python main.py
```

## Controls

### Application

| Action | Control |
|---|---|
| Change mode | Click a top navigation item or press `Tab` |
| Switch theme | Click `Light` or `Dark` in the header |
| Pause a maze or shooter run | `Esc` |
| Exit the application | Close the window |

### Breakpoint

| Action | Control |
|---|---|
| Move | `W` `A` `S` `D` or arrow keys |
| Aim | Mouse |
| Fire | Hold left mouse button or `Space` |
| Dash | `Shift` (cooldown applies) |
| Pause / resume | `Esc` |
| Toggle fullscreen | `F11` |

### Maze

| Action | Control |
|---|---|
| Move / turn | `W` / `S` and `A` / `D` or arrow keys |
| Strafe | `Q` / `E` |
| Look | Drag inside the view |
| Projection | `P` |
| Scan nearby cells | `Space` |
| Pause | `Esc` |
| Continue after a stage | `Enter` or `C` |
| New run | `R` |

### Explore

| Action | Control |
|---|---|
| Choose a mesh | Shape picker |
| Rotate / move | Drag or keyboard controls |
| Scale | Mouse wheel or `+` / `-` |
| Projection / axes | `P` / `X` |
| Load sample OBJ | `O` |
| Reset / screenshot | `R` / `F12` |
| Change render mode | `M` |

## Design

Explore and Challenges use RenderX's own transformation, clipping, projection, and rasterization code. Maze geometry uses the same wireframe path. Breakpoint uses a separate OpenGL 3.3 pipeline for its textured 3D models and real-time combat.

The shooter code and model assets are adapted from [3D-RPG-Shooter](https://github.com/dev-mojammel-hosain/3D-RPG-Shooter) with project-owner authorization. Its original license and a detailed acknowledgement are included in [`renderx/shooter/UPSTREAM.md`](renderx/shooter/UPSTREAM.md).

See [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for the component boundaries and [`docs/REFERENCES.md`](docs/REFERENCES.md) for project credits.
